-The method operates on $3 \times 3$ symmetric covariance matrices. The transformation constructs a local basis matrix.
+*   `basis`: 3x3 matrix where columns are vectors $v_1, v_2, n$.
+*   `cov`: 3x3 intermediate covariance matrix in the basis coordinate system.
+*   `sigma`: 3x3 regularized covariance matrix in the basis coordinate system before transformation back to world space.
 
-**Algorithm Steps:**
-The regularization is applied to the covariance matrix $\Sigma$ to produce $\sigma$. This process is performed every 5000 iterations [S1].
